{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231756-what-benefits-does-just-a-hearthstone-give","id":1231756,"title":"What benefits does just a Hearthstone give?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-02T04:05:56-07:00","id":1231756,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What benefits does just a Hearthstone give?","content":"I'm a little bit unclear on hearthstones in Exalted 3rd edition. If a player buys just the Hearthstone merit (so no Manse, and no Artifact in which to socket the stone), what benefits do they get? I remember 1st Ed Hearthstones being really cool, but I can't quite figure 3e ones out. The rules - which I have read, but which are somewhat sprawling, so I may have just missed something - don't appear to be explicit.<br /> <br /> Some hearthstone descriptions explicitly mention socketing, while some don't - can I assume the latter type don't need it?<br /> <br /> Is there any kind of Essence trickle like in previous editions? In fact, I'm not 100% sure what the rules are on Hearthstone-essence-trickle even if socketed and/or accompanied by Manse ownership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24353-asilano","name":"Asilano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T04:26:30-07:00","id":1231759,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you <i>just</i> get a hearthstone, you'll want one of the ones that just do a thing. No socketing or attunement necessary.<br /> <br /> In 3e hearthstones don't provide mote drip per se. What they do is extend the benefits of standing in a manse they're linked with. This can provide a number of benefits, but as far as mote regeneration goes you essentially get to carry a demesne around with you. You <i>do</i> need it socketed in an artifact to benefit from this feature, even if the standard power doesn't require it.<br /> <br /> What this means is that not all hearthstones can provide mote drip. Wild-born hearthstones don't have a manse, so they're definitely out. Steady ones might also be unable to provide this benefit, even if they come from a manse, because the book says the hearthstone needs to be &quot;linked&quot; and it's not clear if this refers to the keyword. I'm inclined to say it does, because honestly that just makes more sense to me and stops the keyword, which is optional on some stones, from being mostly drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T05:13:01-07:00","id":1231766,"title":"","content":"Point of just the stone is to get powers or evocations from the stone without a manse that requires constant in game upkeep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T07:07:39-07:00","id":1231798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asilano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231756-what-benefits-does-just-a-hearthstone-give#post1231756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little bit unclear on hearthstones in Exalted 3rd edition. ... but I can't quite figure 3e ones out. The rules - which I have read, but which are somewhat sprawling, so I may have just missed something - don't appear to be explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the Hearthstone merit tells you how to gain benefits of standing in a <i>linked manse</i>, if you own one, and these are described under the Demense merit. ... where <i>of course</i> you would think to look ...<br /> <br /> Okay now, it would have been nicer if the merits just referenced chapter nine where everything was collected together for easy reference, but it is not <i>too</i> sprawled. Just rather inconvenient. The Demesne merit is on page 160; the Hearthstone merit is on page 160-161; and the Manse merit on page 163. There's also the rules for Manse and Demesne attunement on page 161. Everything else is on page 603+.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231756-what-benefits-does-just-a-hearthstone-give?p=1231759#post1231759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3e hearthstones don't provide mote drip per se. What they do is extend the benefits of standing in a manse they're linked with. This can provide a number of benefits, but as far as mote regeneration goes you essentially get to carry a demesne around with you. You <i>do</i> need it socketed in an artifact to benefit from this feature, even if the standard power doesn't require it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically the Manse merit specifies that to benefit from this feature, the hearthstone must be <i>linked to a <u>manse</u></i>, and that the <i>manse' owner </i>must place the hearthstone in the <i>socket</i> of an <i>attuned artefact</i>.<br /> <br /> Whether that &quot;linked&quot; is a reference to the <b>linked </b>keyword is ambiguous, thanks to the decision to write game mechanics in natural language, (though like Elfive I'm inclined towards 'yes'), but you must at least <i>own the manse</i>.<br /> <br /> Although manse attunement does allow for a manse to have several owners, I'm calling <i>no-shenanigans</i> on a manse' owner placing her 'stone in <i>someone else's</i> artefact for <i>him</i> to gain the benefits of standing in <i>her</i> manse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 07-02-2018, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T07:25:31-07:00","id":1231802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231756-what-benefits-does-just-a-hearthstone-give?p=1231798#post1231798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although manse attunement does allow for a manse to have several owners, I'm calling <i>no-shenanigans</i> on a manse' owner placing her 'stone in <i>someone else's</i> artefact for <i>him</i> to gain the benefits of standing in <i>her</i> manse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I'd be fine with that, as long as both parties were attuned to the demesne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T07:59:55-07:00","id":1231809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231756-what-benefits-does-just-a-hearthstone-give?p=1231802#post1231802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd be fine with that, as long as both parties were attuned to the demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mostly meant a third party acquiring the 'stoned artefact without ever attuning the manse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T11:03:20-07:00","id":1231876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231756-what-benefits-does-just-a-hearthstone-give?p=1231809#post1231809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I mostly meant a third party acquiring the 'stoned artefact without ever attuning the manse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third party could attune to the artifact but would gain no benefit from hearthstone whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}